{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3299","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3299","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3299\",\"parent_revision\":\"72cbbdb6ab0e24b176d5ef9e0f8d8aec5bd557a19b356c58aa4b71c218aa4fa1\",\"root_revision\":\"72cbbdb6ab0e24b176d5ef9e0f8d8aec5bd557a19b356c58aa4b71c218aa4fa1\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-29\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nFollow-up from #3169 (content-based duplicate detection). `build_concept_query` (backlog_core/search.py) has no domain stopword list, so \\\"backlog\\\" \u2014 a near-universal word in this subsystem's own titles/bodies \u2014 frequently becomes one of only 4 concept terms extracted for the duplicate-match query. Since nearly every existing backlog item's body also contains \\\"backlog\\\", `find_content_duplicates` frequently returns a match_count=1 false positive purely on that one generic word.\\n\\nVerified during #3169's T5 (test authoring) against 7+ real, genuinely-unrelated issue pairs in this repo (e.g. #2978 vs #1664, #916 vs #2585, #694 vs #1076) \u2014 all falsely matched at match_count=1 due to \\\"backlog\\\" alone. T5's shipped AC5 test corpus (12 pairs) passes only because those specific pairs were deliberately chosen to avoid triggering this; the underlying algorithm still has the gap in production.\\n\\nImpact: any new backlog-subsystem item titled with the word \\\"backlog\\\" (extremely common for this subsystem's own feature requests) risks a spurious DuplicateItemError when created via `add_item`'s write-time gate.\\n\\nRecommended fix (not prescriptive \u2014 grooming should confirm the best approach): add \\\"backlog\\\"/\\\"github\\\"/\\\"mcp\\\" (or similarly over-represented domain terms) to a `_CONCEPT_STOPWORDS` set in backlog_core/search.py, or require `match_count >= 2` before treating a candidate as a duplicate.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Quality vigilance concern from #3169\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-29T09:51:03.153708Z</sub>\\n\\n**Partial progress note (2026-08-29):** commit f7d49d9cf (PR #3274, fixing a separate false-negative bug in `build_concept_query`) already added `\\\"backlog\\\"`, `\\\"item\\\"`, and `\\\"during\\\"` to `_CONCEPT_STOPWORDS` in `backlog_core/search.py`, as a side effect of making a stopword change necessary to pass the pinned false-positive regression corpus. This is a real but partial fix for this issue's root cause \u2014 `\\\"backlog\\\"` (the word this issue names) is now stopworded, but this issue's broader ask (a more complete domain stopword list, or a `match_count >= 2` threshold) is still open. Grooming should verify current false-positive behavior against the corpus in tests/test_backlog_core_search.py before deciding whether further work is still needed here.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"341876f44c628549d89055019fb2c8b74f200228ed08779d8bf1cf03cc6e9639\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRYoZ7g\"}"}